## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 65a7383f98f831cf957630ed5750bf2ec7f249cf

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** The fix commit (16840bb) is mostly a large refactor removing `RoundEndData`, but the commit message explicitly says "Also fixes a bug." I traced the history of the files touched to find where a genuine behavioral bug (not just refactoring) was introduced. `TickCounter.java` stood out because its constructor changed in the fix — a line `tickCount = maxTicks;` was removed. I checked `git log --follow` on that file and found it was created from scratch in the immediately preceding commit `65a7383` ("Cleans up and simplifies the game's processing in the session"), which is also where `TickCounter` was first wired into `GameSession`.

**(2) The specific change:** In `65a7383`, `TickCounter`'s constructor set `tickCount = maxTicks;` at the end:
```java
public TickCounter(TickHandler tickHandler, int maxTicks, int tickDuration) {
    this.tickHandler = tickHandler;
    this.maxTicks = maxTicks;
    this.tickDuration = tickDuration;
    tickCount = maxTicks;   // <-- bug
}
